cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use dewata.org in academic work, please cite it using the metadata
  below. customary protocols and ceremony classifications are NOT public
  themselves; this citation covers the calendar engine and DSP v0.1 spec only.
title: "dewata.org — civic infrastructure for Bali's customary ceremony"
abstract: >-
  a deterministic Python engine for Balinese calendrical conversion (Pawukon + Saka + Wewaran + Rahinan),
  with a conformance corpus of 75,000+ vectors and reference DSP v0.1 endpoints.
  designed for adat-first cultural record-keeping, not tourism navigation.
authors:
  - family-names: "de la Rua"
    given-names: "Alejandro"
    email: "warden@usahabali.online"
    affiliation: "dewata.org"
type: software
keywords:
  - balinese
  - pawukon
  - saka
  - wewaran
  - customary
  - banjar
  - cerimonia
  - cultural-sovereignty
license: MIT
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-09-13
repository-code: "https://github.com/consciousclarity/dewata-org"
url: "https://dewata.org"
references:
